cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CliffForge, please cite it as below."
title: "CliffForge: Relative-Affinity Molecular Analogue Prioritization and Activity-Cliff Analysis"
type: software
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-18"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/chidwipak/TELEMEDICON26"
abstract: >-
  CliffForge is an early-stage research prototype for small-molecule lead optimization. It combines
  training-derived matched-molecular-pair analogue generation with a Siamese relative-affinity model,
  uncertainty-aware ranking and activity-cliff analysis, evaluated retrospectively on COVID Moonshot
  SARS-CoV-2 Mpro data. Submitted to the TELEMEDICON26 hackathon by Team Genesis.
keywords:
  - activity cliffs
  - lead optimization
  - relative binding affinity
  - matched molecular pairs
  - SARS-CoV-2 main protease
authors:
  - family-names: "Kuppani"
    given-names: "Chidwipak"
  - family-names: "Kurapati"
    given-names: "Hrishikesh"
